+Candidate citations in the JSON refer to tree `e5b504a6db93a1a72cb79cbac37030ad13a26db1`, never ambient worktree code. Source task AC, `surface-table.md`, producer results, hosted-precheck-1 and handoff-note-2 were obtained read-only by the board CLI. The pinned [Clap 4.5.58 Parser documentation](https://docs.rs/clap/4.5.58/clap/trait.Parser.html#method.parse) confirms that `parse` exits instead of returning on errors; the cleanup-bypass conclusion follows from that API behavior and the inspected ownership call chain. [Rust's Result Termination implementation](https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/process.rs.html) emits an `Error:` prefix, and [Anyhow 1.0.103 formatting](https://docs.rs/anyhow/1.0.103/anyhow/struct.Error.html#display-representations) explains Debug/backtrace output from returning an error through main. Thus the stderr change is a static inference supported by the documented formatter and both unchanged main signatures, not a claimed local binary run.
